      "content": "it's not just about \"unintended byproducts\" though. if it were actually an accident, the math wouldn't be so perfect across different regions. it feels like they're using the grid as a giant tuning fork. even if there's no \"official\" document saying so, you can see the pattern in how specialized signal modulation is used in other ways... if they can use it for communications, why couldn't they use it to influence the collective headspace? it just seems like a massive oversight to say it's physically impossible to layer subtle sub-frequencies over a standard 60hz carrier.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
